-- EXPECT-ERROR: `Cap(IO)` cannot be serialized
-- Capability unforgeability (R3), the ENCODE direction (2026-08-05).
--
-- Encoding a capability leaks nothing at run time — capabilities are opaque
-- unit sentinels and `march_cap_narrow` in runtime/march_runtime.c is
-- literally `return cap;`. This is rejected anyway, for two reasons:
--
--   1. it manufactures the wire value a decoder would consume, so leaving it
--      open keeps half of the round trip alive;
--   2. `derive Json for T` generates BOTH directions from one declaration, so
--      a rule that rejected only decoding would leave the derive half
--      generated — a working encoder beside a rejected decoder.
--
-- One symmetric rule ("`Cap` is not a serializable type") is easier to state,
-- easier to test, and leaves no direction to reopen later.
mod EncodeCap do
  needs IO

  fn main(cap : Cap(IO)) do
    println(to_json(cap))
  end
end
